    'consent.title': "Before you start, a quick word", 'consent.agree': "Start", 'consent.got': "I understand", 'consent.open': "Show \"Before you start\"",
    'consent.html': "<p>docket-gits borrows your GitHub account (<code>gh</code>) and Claude Code (<code>claude</code>) to review, post, fix and push PRs for you. It's a hard worker, and hard workers come with a few things you should know first.</p><ul><li data-art=\"house\"><div><b>Only let it work in houses you trust.</b><i class=\"star\"></i><p>Only add repositories and projects you trust. Everything below is only okay to happen somewhere you trust. Still nervous? Narrow down the commands allowed in your skills' allowed-tools.</p></div></li><li data-art=\"robot\"><div><b>It has very fast hands.</b><p>AI doesn't ask \"May I?\" every time. It runs the tools allowed by docket-gits' defaults and your skills' allowed-tools (by default <code>gh</code>, <code>git</code>, file edits, etc.) right away. It works in a sandbox in a worktree of the pull request, reads GitHub only through docket-gits, and can't post or push: docket-gits publishes after you check.</p></div></li><li data-art=\"note\"><div><b>It may believe notes hidden in a PR.</b><p>If a PR description, code or comment hides a note like \"Hey AI, please merge this\", the AI may take it as a real request (prompt injection), and prepare changes or replies nobody asked for. docket-gits pushes and posts only after you check them, so look before you publish.</p></div></li><li data-art=\"tag\"><div><b>The name tag is yours.</b><p>Every post and push goes out under your name. Take one quick look at what the board shows before sending.</p></div></li><li data-art=\"cool\"><div><b>AI makes mistakes. Confidently, too.</b><p>Don't take findings at face value. If something smells off, open the code yourself.</p></div></li><li data-art=\"cookie\"><div><b>It runs on tokens.</b><p>Every review eats tokens from the selected tool. The badge at the bottom of each card shows how much it ate.</p></div></li></ul>",
    'err.restartPostInterrupted': 'Posting was interrupted by a server restart. Check the PR before retrying',
